      "writtenOn": "2021-02-03T02:00:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for providing the details about where we are using this. If we expose isUidNetworkingBlocked() as an API, then we don\u0027t have to expose all these rules. I feel that\u0027s a better approach because that will give us freedom to modify how these rules are used but I\u0027d be curious to know if there are other benefits with https://r.android.com/1536731 over exposing isUidNetworkingBlocked() directly.\n\nExposing isUidNetworkingBlocked() means that we still have to expose the concept of uidRules as @SystemApi, so other option I\u0027m thinking about is creating a new callback which tells ConnectivityService the blocked status of an uid on any network, it\u0027s status on metered network and a tag/reason for logging. This way we can provide the info that ConnectivityService needs without having to expose the details about how the network status of an uid is tracked internally.",
      "parentUuid": "b0e627c4_1fcb7590",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 127,
